<title>USA: Harley-Davidson ordered to pay $9.9 mln.</title>
<headline>Harley-Davidson ordered to pay $9.9 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harley-Davidson Inc said Thursday a New Jersey Court ordered the company to pay $9.9 million in compensatory damages, plus interest, in a product liability lawsuit.</p>
<p>The company said the suit, filed in Superior Court of New Jersey, stemmed from a 1991 motorcycle accident.</p>
<p>Harley-Davidson officials were unavailable to comment on whether the company plans to appeal the damage award.</p>
<p>Harley-Davidson produces heavyweight motorcycles and associated motorcycle parts.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
